  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-06-05T01:03:46.635Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If this is intended behavior for some reason, then the attached tooltip should probably be changed to reflect that. But as it stands now, what unfortunately occurs is all the kicked users will congregate in one other public instance, greeting any unsuspecting harmless users with the terrible behavior they were all kicked for, while also bad-mouthing the mod team & spreading false rumors, etc. etc. It's quite dystopian...\n\nTo clarify, this happens when I kick people from my own world that I uploaded. I'm currently unsure if this issue extends to moderators kicking from Group Public instances.",
